title: "PoroMechanics.jl: Reactive transport and poromechanics of porous media"
abstract: "Simulation of coupled phenomena in porous media: unsaturated flow (Richards, Darcy), solute diffusion, non-isothermal drying coupling liquid water, dry air and heat, Biot poroelasticity, and multi-ionic reactive transport in cementitious materials with thermodynamic equilibrium from cemdata18. Physics models are declared as plain structs implementing a small callback interface, on two numerical backends: finite volumes (VoronoiFVM.jl) for transport, finite elements (Ferrite.jl) for coupled mechanics. Jacobians are obtained by automatic differentiation rather than written by hand."
keywords:
  - "porous media"
  - "Julia"
  - "reactive transport"
  - "poromechanics"
  - "unsaturated flow"
  - "finite volume method"
  - "finite element method"
  - "cement"
  - "chloride ingress"
version: "0.1.0"
# date-released and doi are filled in at release time, once the Zenodo DOI exists.
